Feature: Mission commands
  Each item in the plan is a [[MAVLink]] mission command. The plan shows its short name, for
  example WAYPOINT for MAV_CMD_NAV_WAYPOINT. These commands fly the plane to a point:
  WAYPOINT, LOITER_UNLIM, LOITER_TURNS, LAND and RTL. LOITER_UNLIM circles until you give a
  new command, and LOITER_TURNS circles a set number of times. When you change the command
  of an item, the item stays in its place in the plan.

  Expectation: Changing a command keeps the item in its place
    Given the plan has at least 1 item
    When the last plan item is LOITER_TURNS
    Then the plan stays the same

  Expectation: Changing a command makes the vehicle's copy out of date
    Given the plan has at least 1 item
    And the vehicle mission is up to date
    When the last plan item is LAND
    Then the vehicle mission is out of date
